      "After adding it, open \"Manage Project\" for your project (\"Manage\" in ALCOM) and install the packages you want.",
    ],
    casesTitle: "Common problems",
    caseLabels: { symptom: "What happens", fix: "How to fix it" },
    cases: [
      { title: "Unity Hub recommends a newer version",
        symptom: "Unity Hub keeps recommending that you install a newer version. Older versions show a security warning.",
        fix: `Close it without installing. Keep your VRChat projects on ${unityVersion}. VRChat also says this warning doesn't apply to VRChat avatars and worlds.` },
      { title: "It says Unity can't be found",
        symptom: "VCC or ALCOM says Unity can't be found. Projects won't open.",
        fix: `Check in Unity Hub that ${unityVersion} is installed. If it is, set the Unity location: in VCC, under Unity Editors in "Settings"; in ALCOM, with "Add Unity" in "Settings". ALCOM may also find it after you restart it.` },
      { title: "Unity won't open because of a license error",
